(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/cachedParser.asl#parseCachedForm" :text "PARSER-inferredUnitConsumers / INFERUNIT round 2: a cached AST handed back to a caller that renders it (e.g. for a cache-hit diff or re-emission) must not leak the :inferredUnit sentinel, so it is dropped before the node is cached. Delegated to ip/stripInferredUnit (asl-parser/indentParser, which also defines the sentinel) rather than keeping a private copy; the prior copy here matched (rd/sexprHead h) on any SExpr, atom or list, and kept scanning past the header into the body, so a body form like (:inferredUnit 1) false-matched and lost real body forms")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/fnHeader.asl#" :text "Pure string/list primitives for folding a fn declaration's indented param-list continuation (name: or -> lines) back onto its header line. Shared by asl-parser/ast (per-top-node text, via the CST) and asl-parser/indentParser (whole-file text, with its own string-literal and position-remap handling), so there is exactly one copy of the join rule. Imports only builtins, so either module can depend on it without a cycle.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/fnHeader.asl#stripCrLine" :text "The line without one trailing carriage return.")
