(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#parseIndented" :text "Parses an indented source string into a single S-expression.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#stripInferredUnit" :text "Drops the synthetic -> :inferredUnit pair parseFnParamsAndReturn inserts for a no-arrow fn header, leaving everything else (params, docstring, body) untouched, so a canonical renderer never leaks the sentinel.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#isDotAccessorAtom?" :text "a module header's path atom and each import pair's lead path, such as bench.aep.ablation, are dotted package paths, never field-access expressions; desugarDot (run on every bare symbol token, including these) folds them into nested (.-field base) member-chain forms, which checkModPath/importPair then read as just their outermost .-field head, losing every earlier segment. Since a module header never holds a real expression, any member-chain shape anywhere inside one is always a misdesugared path and is safe to fold back to its original dotted atom.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#schemaFieldsLoop" :text "a field type may be a delimited group")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#leadingSpaceCount" :text "count a line's leading plain spaces (tabs already become spaces by W001 before this text is built from tracked-file lines)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#buildHeaderSegmentsLoop" :text "replays fh/headerJoin's \"header + ' ' + trim(line)\" accumulation to record where each consumed line's content landed in the joined text, so a diagnostic column inside the joined header can be mapped back to its true line:col")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#remapErrorPos" :text "only fn headers that were actually joined have a table entry; every other diagnostic line:col passes through unchanged")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#fnHeaderScanLine" :text "tracks whether each line starts inside an open string literal carried from a prior line, so a line that only looks like a fn header because it sits inside a multi-line string is never joined")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#takeNonStringLines" :text "a continuation search must not cross into a line that starts inside an open string: truncate the lookahead there so headerJoin only ever sees real code")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#joinFnHeaderContinuations" :text "a top-level fn whose param list continues on an indented next line is joined onto the header line before tokenizing, one blank line per joined line so later line numbers hold, so the indent lexer never sees a header block deeper than the function body; skips any line starting inside an open string, and returns a line:col remap table for diagnostics that land inside a joined header")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/src/indentParser.asl#dropInferredArrowPair" :text "INFERUNIT round 2: the one place that knows the :inferredUnit sentinel's exact shape (an atom -> immediately followed by an atom :inferredUnit, placed by parseFnParamsAndReturn right after the params vector) is here, so every consumer calls this instead of keeping its own copy. The prior two copies matched (rd/sexprHead h) on any SExpr, atom or list, so a body form like (-> x) or (:inferredUnit 1) false-matched, and they kept recursing past the header into the body; this one requires both slots to be bare atoms and stops looking the moment it finds the first -> atom, matched or not, so nothing past the header is ever touched")
