(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astConverterTest.asl#" :text "Falsifiable test suite for Task 52605 Bidirectional AST Converter and Roundtrip Equivalence.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astConverterTest.asl#testTypedLetBindings" :text "A typed let binding (name Type expr) survives lift then lower in every binding wrapper.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astConverterTest.asl#runTests" :text "Runs the converter roundtrip and top-form suites.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astNativeBuildTest.asl#" :text "The typed AST converter and printer compile natively: asl1 builds fixtures/nativeAstSuites.asl, which runs astConverterTest and astPrinterTest, clang links the .ll against libaslrt.a and the program exits 42. Runs asl-host, clang and the program through processRun in a fresh temporary directory.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astNodeTest.asl#" :text "Falsifiable test suite for Task 52604 Typed AST Hierarchy AstExpr, AstPattern, and AstType Definitions.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#" :text "Falsifiable test suite for Task 52606 Canonical Indented AST Formatter astPrinter.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testTypedBindingPrinting" :text "A lifted typed binding prints its type annotation and value, never the internal :typed marker.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#runTests" :text "Runs the typed AST printer suites.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testHostDialectTopForms" :text "printed modules must load in asl-host: brackets in let and fn slots, corpus header keys, parenthesized calls, doc lines, ?-suffixed keywords")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testEffectMarkerAndTryGuard" :text "the fn effect marker and the keyword-only guard of the try reversal are invisible to asl-host check, so they are pinned textually")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testUntypedParamBeforeTyped" :text "PRINTER-untypedParam: an untyped param ahead of a typed one, such as fn f text n: Int64, must keep both params distinct through parse, print and reparse, never folding the next param's name in as the first one's type")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testInferredReturnTypeNoArrow" :text "INT16-printerValid: a fn header with no -> at all lets the host infer the real return type from the body; indentParser.asl used to default this to the atom Unit regardless, so astPrinter always printed an explicit -> Unit that fails asl-host check against a String-returning body. indentParser now marks this case with the :inferredUnit sentinel and astPrinter omits the arrow and type entirely, reproducing the original no-arrow header.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testDottedModulePath" :text "INT16-printerValid (bench/aep/tests/ablationTest.asl): a module header written with dots in its path and import, such as bench.aep.ablation, is a package path, not a member-access expression; desugarDot used to fold it into a nested (.-field base) chain regardless, and checkModPath/importPair then read only the chain's outermost head, collapsing bench.aep.tests.ablationTest down to .-ablationTest. indentParser now repairs any member-chain shape found inside a module header back to its flat dotted atom.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testInlineEnumCasePrinting" :text "PRINTENUM: an inline single-line enum (cases on the enum header line, no { } and no indented block) must canonicalize each bare (name) case into a (:case name [] doc) form while parsing, like the brace and indented-block forms already do; before the fix the raw (name) group was kept verbatim and asl-host rejected it with 'every defenum member must be a (:case ...) form'")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testInlineSchemaFieldPrinting" :text "PRINTENUM: an inline single-line schema (fields on the schema header line, no { } and no indented block) must canonicalize each field, bare x: Type or parenthesized (y Type), into a (:field name Type doc) form while parsing, like the brace and indented-block forms already do; before the fix the whole line was kept as one raw call and asl-host rejected the printed form with 'every defschema member must be a (:field ...) form' (or, for an all-bare-token line, 'defschema needs at least one field' since no sub-form was a parenthesized list at all)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testInlineEnumCaseFieldsDocOrder" :text "PRINTENUM: inline enum cases keep their typed fields (name: Type, colon intact), their trailing docstrings and their source order; before the fix the standalone : tokens were filtered out first, so (box value: Int64) printed as [(value Any) (Int64 Any)]")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testInlineEnumCaseFormPassthrough" :text "PRINTENUM: an inline enum whose cases are already written as (:case ...) or (:c ...) forms passes them through unchanged, and a standalone : after the enum name is skipped as before; before the fix the :case keyword was taken as the case name and the rest as fields, printing an unreparsable [(red Any) ([ Any) (] Any) ...] vector")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/astPrinterTest.asl#testArraySugarParamPrinting" :text "PRINTARRPARAM: a fn param typed with [Type] array sugar, name: [Type] on its own (no enclosing parens around the param list), must keep that name and type through parse, print and reparse; parseOneParamToks only special-cased a ( type start after the colon, taking a balanced group, and fell through to treating a lone [ token as the whole type (consuming just that one token) for anything else, so [Str] desugared into three bogus params (name '['), (name 'Str', type Any), (name ']', type Any) and the printed signature lost the real name and type entirely; a second param after the [Str] group pins where parsing resumes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/balanceTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for pure AgentSlang delimiter balance and structural verification engine.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cachedParserTest.asl#" :text "Hermetic verification suite for Content-Addressed Subtree AST Caching (Phase 563)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cachedParserTest.asl#testCachedParserNoArrowFnDropsSentinel" :text "PARSER-inferredUnitConsumers: indentParser.asl's parseFnParamsAndReturn marks a no-arrow fn header with the :inferredUnit sentinel; a cached AST rendered back out (as any caller of parseCachedForm might, for a diff or re-emission) must not leak that internal sentinel. formText is bare indent-dialect text (no enclosing parens) since that is what triggers the bare-'fn'-token dispatch in indentParser.asl's parseTopForm and so the parseFnParamsAndReturn path that produces the sentinel")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cachedParserTest.asl#testCachedParserArrowedFnBodyNotCorrupted" :text "INFERUNIT round 2: a prior dropInferredArrowPair matched (rd/sexprHead h) on any SExpr (atom or list) and kept scanning past the real header into the body, so a real-arrow fn whose body happens to contain (-> x) or (:inferredUnit 1) lost those body forms entirely; this fn has a genuine -> Int64 header, so nothing should be dropped at all")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cachedParserTest.asl#testCachedParserParenFnWithNoArrowKeepsListShapedBody" :text "INFERUNIT round 3: testCachedParserArrowedFnBodyNotCorrupted never exercises dropInferredArrowPair's own isAtom? guards, because the header's genuine -> atom always stops the scan before it reaches the body's list-shaped (-> x). code here is a bare paren form (no indent-dialect fn header line at all), so parseFnParamsAndReturn never runs and no sentinel is inserted; its first two items after params ARE the body's (-> x) and (:inferredUnit 1) lists. Removing either isAtom? guard matches a list head the same as the atom and drops the whole body")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cachedParserTest.asl#testCachedParserArrowedFnBareSentinelAtomsInBodySurvive" :text "INFERUNIT round 3: testCachedParserArrowedFnBodyNotCorrupted never exercises the stop-at-first-mismatch behaviour either, since its body forms are lists and can never satisfy dropInferredArrowPair's own atom match regardless of whether the scan continues past them. A real -> Int64 header followed by two bare atoms -> and :inferredUnit as plain body forms is the one shape where continuing to scan past the header's non-matching -> Int64 would reach and wrongly strip them")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/commentEradicationTest.asl#" :text "Comments read as asl-host reads them: ';' to end of line is dropped by both lexers, ';' inside a string is kept, '#' starts a comment only as a line's first character and is otherwise a symbol character.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/conformanceTest.asl#" :text "20-adversarial conformance suite for ASL v0.4 hardened lexer and parser (ADR D81, D77).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheProbe.asl#" :text "Fixture for corpusCacheTest: runs the per-file checks of the suites named in CORPUS_CACHE_PROBE_SUITES (layoutCorpus printReparse liftLower; all when unset) over the space-separated paths in CORPUS_CACHE_PROBE_FILES with the cache from ASL_CORPUS_CACHE, one assertion per file and suite plus one stats report per layoutCorpus and printReparse")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#" :text "Gate for the corpus verdict cache (unit corpusIncremental): a second run over a fixed file set hits the cache for every file with identical runner assertion counts; changing one asl-parser/src file in a copied root invalidates every entry; a file whose content changes is re-checked; a broken file is never cached; opening the cache evicts fingerprint dirs idle for 7 days and keeps recently used ones")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#runnerCounts" :text "the runner's executed and passed counts")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testSecondRunHits!" :text "part 1: warm run hits every file, counts unchanged")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testDefaultSnapshotCache!" :text "default HOME cache survives separate gate snapshot working directories; edits still miss")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testMissingRootsDisableCache!" :text "missing fingerprint roots never authorize shared verdict reuse")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testDefaultRootCoverage!" :text "known source files in the cache-using suite import closure stay fingerprinted")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testParserChangeInvalidates!" :text "part 2: one parser source edit invalidates everything")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testContentChangeRechecks!" :text "part 3: changed content is re-checked, not served")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testBrokenNeverCached!" :text "part 4: a failing file never reaches the cache")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/corpusCacheTest.asl#testSharedFingerprintsRetained!" :text "part 5: live fingerprints kept, idle ones evicted")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cstBridgeTest.asl#" :text "CST lowering bridge tests for span preservation and indented misparse fixes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cstBridgeTest.asl#allKidsHaveOffsets?" :text "check if all kid forms have end offsets")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cstBridgeTest.asl#findEnumByName" :text "find first enum node by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cstBridgeTest.asl#findSchemaByName" :text "find first schema node by name")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/cstBridgeTest.asl#runTests" :text "test CST bridge and misparse fixes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/destructuringTest.asl#" :text "Falsifiable test suite for Task 52602 Record and List Pattern Destructuring in Let and Function Bindings.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/desugarHostTest.asl#" :text "The host is the oracle for desugared forms: asl-host eval runs what list destructuring and the try operator lower to and must print the value the source means. Runs asl-host through processRun from the workspace root.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/dyck1BalanceTest.asl#" :text "D81 acceptance gate fixture for Task 54801: asl-parser Dyck-1 Reader, Balance & Converter Unification.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/edgeCaseTest.asl#" :text "Dual-polarity edge-case verification for Task 54503: Parser Hardening & Macro Anomaly Triage.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/enumCaseFieldsTest.asl#" :text "Enum case fields come out the same from both dialects. The fn-dialect parser writes a [ ] vector as (list ...); a case's field vector must not gain a nameless field from that list head.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/fnHeaderJoinTest.asl#" :text "A fn header whose parameters continue on indented lines is joined onto one line (plan SH unit NB3) and keeps the line count, so the native checker reports a body diagnostic at its source line")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/fsmBench.asl#" :text "Deterministic performance and accumulator purity benchmark for polyglot FSM scanner")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/fsmTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for polyglot streaming FSM outline scanner under strict falsification")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/grammarTrieTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for in-memory grammar trie constrained decoding under strict falsification")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentLexerTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for pure ASL v0.4 Indentation-Aware Lexer (Item 1.1, Task T11_LEXER_V04).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentLexerTest.asl#testMultiLineStringLiteral" :text "A6c: a newline inside a string literal joins the literal text, as asl-host's reader accepts; this reference lexer used to split the source into lines up front and report unterminated string literal instead")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentLexerTest.asl#testManyEscapesLinear" :text "decodeLoop joined the decoded prefix at every escape, quadratic on a long escaped literal (shard3 hang)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentParserTest.asl#" :text "Unit tests for pure ASL v0.4 Syntactic Parser & Closed-Vocabulary Desugaring (Item 1.2, Task T12_PARSER_V04).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentParserTest.asl#testFnHeaderJoinSkipsStringLiteral" :text "round 2 item 1: a multi-line string literal whose body happens to contain a column-0 'fn x ...' line followed by an indented 'b: ...' line must not be mistaken for a real continuable header; the string's content must survive byte-for-byte")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentParserTest.asl#testFnHeaderJoinErrorPositionRemap" :text "round 2 item 2: an error produced from inside a joined header's continuation segment must report the continuation's own original line:col, not the merged header line's")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentParserTest.asl#testFnHeaderJoinStripsCr" :text "round 2 item 4: a CRLF line ending on the header line must not land embedded mid-token in the joined header")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentPrinterTest.asl#" :text "Falsifiable gate for pure ASL v0.4 Canonical Formatter (Item 2.1, Task T21_CANONICAL_FORMATTER_V04).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentProjectionTest.asl#" :text "D81 acceptance gate fixture for Task 54804: astPrinter & indentPrinter Lossless Indented Projection.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/indentReaderIntegrationTest.asl#" :text "Baseline integration tests for Language v0.4 pure ASL indented reader.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/lexerTest.asl#" :text "Execution driver for the self-hosted lexer: tokenize a sample.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/lexerTest.asl#oneTokenKind" :text "ASL1-floatExponentLiteral: the kind of the single token tokenizing s should yield, before its trailing EOF.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/lexerTest.asl#oneTokenFloat" :text "ASL1-floatExponentLiteral: the Float64 value of the single FLOAT token tokenizing s should yield, or 0.0 when it is not one.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/lexerTest.asl#testExponentFloats" :text "ASL1-floatExponentLiteral: 1e22, 1.5e-3 and -2E+5 lex as one FLOAT token each, not a split INT/SYMBOL pair, with the exponent folded into the parsed value; an incomplete exponent (1e, 1e+) is one ERROR token, not a silent fallback to a bare int plus a symbol.")
